The UE shall:

- continue using the configuration used prior to when the inability to comply with the RRCReconfiguration message was detected;  
- continue using the configuration used prior to the reception of RRCReconfiguration message.

Upon reception of RRCReject, the UE shall:

- stop timer T300, if running;
- stop timer T319, if running;
- stop timer T319a, if running;
- stop timer T302, if running;
- reset MAC and release the default MAC Cell Group configuration;
- if waitTime is configured in the RRCReject: start timer T302 with the timer value set to the waitTime;
- if RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: inform the upper layer that access barring is applicable for all access categories except categories '0' and '2';
- if RRCReject is received in response to an RRCSetupRequest: inform upper layers about the failure to setup the RRC connection, upon which the procedure ends;
- else if RRCReject is received in response to an RRCResumeRequest or an RRCResumeRequest1:
  - if resume is triggered by upper layers: inform upper layers about the failure to resume the RRC connection;
  - if resume is triggered due to an RNA update; or
  - if resume is triggered for SDT and T380 is not running: set the variable pendingRNA-Update to true;
  - discard the current K_gNB*, K_RRCenc, K_RRCint, K_UPenc, K_UPint keys derived in accordance with 5.3.13.3;
  - suspend SRB1 and the radio bearers configured for SDT, if any;
  - for each radio bearer configured for SDT: indicate PDCP suspend to lower layers; re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;
  - the procedure ends.

Additionally, the RRC_INACTIVE UE shall continue to monitor paging while timer T302 is running.

The UE shall:  
- remove the entry with the matching measObjectId from the measObjectList within the VarMeasConfig;  
- remove all measId associated with this measObjectId from the measIdList within the VarMeasConfig, if any;  
- if a measId is removed from the measIdList:  
  - remove the measurement reporting entry for this measId from the VarMeasReportList, if included;  
  - stop the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322, whichever is running, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId.

For each condReconfigId received in the condReconfigToAddModList IE, the UE shall:

- if an entry with the matching condReconfigId exists in the condReconfigToAddModList within the VarConditionalReconfig:
  - if the entry includes a condExecutionCond or condExecutionCondSCG, replace the corresponding value in VarConditionalReconfig;
  - if the entry includes a condRRCReconfig, replace condRRCReconfig in VarConditionalReconfig;
  - add a new entry for this condReconfigId within the VarConditionalReconfig;
- perform conditional reconfiguration evaluation as specified in 5.3.5.13.4.

The UE shall:

- Store handover failure information in VarRLF-Report according to 5.3.10.5;
- Revert back to the configuration used in the source PCell;
- Initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in clause 5.3.7.

Upon reception of RRCReject, the UE is required to execute the following actions (per TS 38.331, clause 5.3.4 — “RRC connection rejection”):

- Stop timer T300, if running;  
- Stop timer T319, if running;  
- Stop timer T319a, if running;  
- Stop timer T302, if running;  
- Reset MAC and release the default MAC Cell Group configuration;  
- If `waitTime` is configured in the RRCReject: start timer T302 with that value;  
- If RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: inform upper layers that access barring is applicable for all access categories **except** categories '0' and '2';  
- If RRCReject is received in response to an RRCSetupRequest: inform upper layers about the failure to setup the RRC connection;  
- If RRCReject is received in response to an RRCResumeRequest or RRCResumeRequest1:  
  - If resume is triggered by upper layers: inform upper layers about the failure to resume the RRC connection;  
  - If resume is triggered due to an RNA update, **or** for SDT and T380 is not running: set `pendingRNA-Update` to `true`;  
  - Discard the current K<sub>gNB</sub>, K<sub>UPenc</sub>, K<sub>UPint</sub>, K<sub>RRCenc</sub>, K<sub>RRCint</sub> keys;  
  - Suspend SRB1 and any radio bearers configured for SDT;  
  - For each SDT-configured radio bearer: indicate PDCP suspend to lower layers and re-establish the RLC entity per TS 38.322.

Additionally, the RRC_INACTIVE UE shall continue to monitor paging while T302 is running.

For each reportConfigId included in the received reportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfig, the UE shall:

- remove the entry with the matching reportConfigId from the reportConfigList within the VarMeasConfig;
- remove all measId associated with the reportConfigId from the measIdList within the VarMeasConfig, if any;
- if a measId is removed from the measIdList:
  - remove the measurement reporting entry for this measId from the VarMeasReportList, if included;
  - stop the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322, whichever one is running, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId.

The UE shall:

- release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3;
- release the corresponding logical channel.

Upon receiving a PUCCH release request from lower layers, for all bandwidth parts of an indicated serving cell the UE shall:  
- release PUCCH-CSI-Resources configured in CSI-ReportConfig;  
- release SchedulingRequestResourceConfig instances configured in PUCCH-Config.

The UE shall reconfigure the sidelink logical channel in accordance with the received `sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5`.

This is explicitly stated in the context:

> For each sl-RLC-ChannelID-PC5 received in the sl-RLC-ChannelToAddModList-PC5 IE the UE shall:  
> 1 > if the current configuration contains a sidelink RLC bearer with the received sl-RLC-ChannelID-PC5:  
> 2 > reconfigure the sidelink RLC entity or entities in accordance with the received sl-RLC-ConfigPC5;  
> **2 > reconfigure the sidelink logical channel in accordance with the received sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5**;

If a UE in RRC_INACTIVE has joined one or more MBS sessions indicated by the TMGI included in the pagingGroupList and none of the ue-Identity in any PagingRecord matches the UE identity allocated by upper layers, it shall initiate the RRC connection resumption procedure according to 5.3.13 with resumeCause set as follows:

- if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 1: resumeCause is set to mps-PriorityAccess;
- else if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 2: resumeCause is set to mcs-PriorityAccess;
- else if the UE is configured by upper layers with one or more Access Identities equal to 11-15: resumeCause is set to highPriorityAccess;
- otherwise, resumeCause is set to mt-Access.

This is based on the exact statement from the context:
> 1 > if in RRC_INACTIVE and the UE has joined one or more MBS session(s) indicated by the TMGI included in the pagingGroupList; and  
> 1 > if none of the ue-Identity included in any of the PagingRecord, if included in the Paging message, matches the UE identity allocated by upper layers:  
> 2 > initiate the RRC connection resumption procedure according to 5.3.13 with resumeCause set as below:  
> 3 > if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 1:  
> 4 > resumeCause is set to mps-PriorityAccess;  
> 3 > else if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 2:  
> 4 > resumeCause is set to mcs-PriorityAccess;  
> 3 > else if the UE is configured by upper layers with one or more Access Identities equal to 11-15:  
> 4 > resumeCause is set to highPriorityAccess;  
> 4 > resumeCause is set to mt-Access.

The UE shall:  
- stop T390 for all access categories;  
- perform the actions as specified in 5.3.14.4.

For a periodical report on an E-UTRA cell where rsrp is set to true, the sorting quantity is RSRP.

This is derived from the context:
> 2 > determine the sorting quantity according to reportQuantity for an E-UTRA cell, as below:  
> 3 > if a single quantity is set to true:  
> 4 > consider this quantity as the sorting quantity;  
> 4 > if rsrp is set to true;  
> 5 > consider RSRP as the sorting quantity;

Since rsrp is set to true and it is the only quantity specified (single quantity), it is considered the sorting quantity.

Upon T311 expiry, if the procedure was initiated due to radio link failure or handover failure, the UE shall:

1. set the noSuitableCellFound in the VarRLF-Report to true;  
2. perform the actions upon going to RRC_IDLE as specified in 5.3.11, with release cause 'RRC connection failure'.

The UE shall:  
1 > for each sl-ReportConfigId included in the received sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL:  
2 > remove the entry with the matching sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-ReportConfigList within the VarMeasConfigSL;  
2 > remove all sl-MeasId associated with the sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any;  
2 > if a sl-MeasId is removed from the sl-MeasIdList:  
3 > remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;  
3 > stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.

The UE stops the periodical reporting timer and resets the associated information (e.g., sl-TimeToTrigger) for each sl-MeasId associated with the modified sl-MeasObjectId.

This is stated in the context under the “sl-MeasObjectToAddModList” handling clause:

> The UE shall: 1 > for each sl-MeasObjectId included in the received sl-MeasObjectToAddModList:  
> 2 > if an entry with the matching sl-MeasObjectId exists in the sl-MeasObjectList within the VarMeasConfigSL, for this entry:  
> 3 > for each sl-MeasId associated with this sl-MeasObjectId included in the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any:  
> 4 > remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;  
> 4 > stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId;  
> 3 > reconfigure the entry with the value received for this sl-MeasObject;  
> 3 > add a new entry for the received sl-MeasObject to the sl-MeasObjectList within VarMeasConfigSL.

If the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by response to NG-RAN paging, the UE shall:

- select '0' as the Access Category;
- perform the unified access control procedure as specified in 5.3.14 using the selected Access Category and one or more Access Identities provided by upper layers;
- if the access attempt is barred, the procedure ends.

When conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled, the UE shall:

- consider the resume procedure is initiated for SDT;  
- start timer T319a;  
- start timer T319;  
- instruct the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running.

This is based on the exact statement from the provided context:  
"1 > if conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled:  
2 > consider the resume procedure is initiated for SDT;  
2 > start timer T319a;  
2 > start timer T319;  
2 > instruct the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running;"

A UE in (NG)EN-DC executes a subclause of clause 5 when:

- it is referred to from a subclause under execution, either in this specification or in TS 36.331;  
- it applies to a message received on SRB3 (if SRB3 is established);  
- it applies to field(s), IE(s), UE variable(s) or timer(s) in this specification that the UE is configured with.

The UE considers the barring for Access Category '2' to be alleviated. If the Access Category was informed to upper layers as barred, the UE informs upper layers about barring alleviation for the Access Category. Additionally, since barring is alleviated for Access Category '2', the UE performs actions specified in 5.3.13.8.

Quote from the context:
> else if timer T390 corresponding to the Access Category '2' expires or is stopped: 2 > consider the barring for this Access Category to be alleviated; 1 > barring for an Access Category is considered being alleviated: 2 > if the Access Category was informed to upper layers as barred: 3 > inform upper layers about barring alleviation for the Access Category. 2 > if barring is alleviated for Access Category '2': 3 > perform actions specified in 5.3.13.8;

If T304 of the MCG expires and any DAPS bearer is configured **without** radio link failure detected in the source PCell, the UE shall:

- release dedicated preambles provided in `rach-ConfigDedicated`, if configured;  
- release dedicated msgA PUSCH resources provided in `rach-ConfigDedicated`, if configured;  
- reset MAC for the target PCell and release the MAC configuration for the target PCell;  
- for each DAPS bearer:  
  - release the RLC entity or entities (as per TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3) and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;  
  - reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS (as per TS 38.323);  
- for each SRB:  
  - if `masterKeyUpdate` was not received:  
    - configure the PDCP entity for the source PCell with state variables continuation (as per TS 38.323);  
  - release the PDCP entity for the target PCell;  
  - release the RLC entity (as per TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3) and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;  
  - trigger the PDCP entity for the source PCell to perform SDU discard (as per TS 38.323);  
  - re-establish the RLC entity for the source PCell;  
- release the physical channel configuration for the target PCell;  
- discard the keys used in the target PCell (i.e., `K_gNB-RRCenc`, `K_gNB-RRCint`, `K_gNB-UPenc`, `K_gNB-UPint`, and `K_gNB-RRCenc` — note: spec text has duplication/typo in key naming, but intent is to discard all target PCell keys);  
- resume suspended SRBs in the source PCell;  
- revert back to the UE configuration used for the DRB or multicast MRB in the source PCell, including PDCP/RLC state variables, security configuration, and data in transmission/reception buffers;  
- revert back to the UE measurement configuration used in the source PCell;  
- store the handover failure information in `VarRLF-Report` (as per clause 5.3.10.5);  
- initiate the failure information procedure (clause 5.7.5) to report DAPS handover failure;  
- revert back to the UE configuration used in the source PCell.

This is directly derived from the first excerpt in the context, specifically the branch:  
> *"The UE shall: 1 > if T304 of the MCG expires, or ... 2 > if any DAPS bearer is configured, and radio link failure is not detected in the source PCell, according to clause 5.3.10.3: 3 > reset MAC for the target PCell and release the MAC configuration for the target PCell; ... [etc.]"*

The UE shall initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration with sync failure, and then initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in clause 5.3.7.

This is derived from the context:
> else if T304 of a secondary cell group expires:  
> 2 > if MCG transmission is not suspended:  
> 3 > release dedicated preambles provided in rach-ConfigDedicated, if configured;  
> 3 > initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration with sync failure, upon which the RRC reconfiguration procedure ends;  
> 3 > if the UE is in NR-DC:  
> 4 > initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in clause 5.3.7;

The three conditions are:

1. The UE is receiving or interested to receive this service via a broadcast MRB;  
2. The session of this service is ongoing or about to start;  
3. One or more MBS FSAIs in the USD for this service is included in SIB21 acquired from the PCell for a frequency belonging to the set of MBS frequencies of interest, determined according to 5.9.4.3.

The Sidelink RRC reconfiguration procedure modifies:

- Establish/modify/release sidelink DRBs;
- (Re-)configure NR sidelink measurement and reporting;
- (Re-)configure sidelink CSI reference signal resources and CSI reporting latency bound;
- Modify parameters included in SLRB-Config of sidelink DRBs associated with the peer UE;
- Establish/modify/release PC5 Relay RLC channels for L2 U2N Relay UE and Remote UE;
- (Re-)configure the peer UE to perform sidelink DRX.

The IAB-node shall:

1. If reestablishRLC is received:  
   - Re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;  
2. Reconfigure the RLC entity or entities in accordance with the received rlc-Config;  
3. Reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac-LogicalChannelConfig.

The UE shall:  
2 > stop timer T331;  
2 > perform the actions as specified in 5.7.8.3.

If the UE is in RRC_IDLE and unable to acquire the MIB, it shall:

- consider the cell as barred in accordance with TS 38.304;
- perform barring as if intraFreqReselection is set to allowed.

This is directly stated in the first context excerpt:  
"if the UE is in RRC_IDLE or in RRC_INACTIVE or in RRC_CONNECTED while T311 is running:  
 if the UE is unable to acquire the MIB:  
  consider the cell as barred in accordance with TS 38.304;  
  perform barring as if intraFreqReselection is set to allowed;"

When the RRCReconfiguration includes daps-SourceRelease, for each DAPS bearer:

- Release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;
- Reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323.

When the RRCReconfiguration includes `daps-SourceRelease`, for each SRB the UE shall:

- **release the PDCP entity for the source SpCell**;  
- **release the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell**.

This is explicitly stated in the context:

> 1 > if the RRCReconfiguration includes the daps-SourceRelease:  
> 2 > reset the source MAC and release the source MAC configuration;  
> 2 > for each DAPS bearer:  
> 3 > release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322 , clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;  
> 3 > reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323 ;  
> 2 > for each SRB:  
> 3 > **release the PDCP entity for the source SpCell**;  
> 3 > **release the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322 , clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell**;  
> 2 > release the physical channel configuration for the source SpCell;  
> 2 > discard the keys used in the source SpCell [...]

The UE shall:

1. > if this procedure was initiated due to reception of the sk-Counter (UE is in NE-DC, or NR-DC, or is configured with SN terminated bearer(s)):  
2 &gt; derive or update the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) based on the KgNB key and using the received sk-Counter value, as specified in TS 33.501 ;  
2 &gt; derive the K<sub>RRCenc</sub> and the K<sub>UPenc</sub> keys as specified in TS 33.501 using the ciphering algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse;  
2 &gt; derive the K<sub>RRCint</sub> and the K<sub>UPint</sub> keys as specified in TS 33.501 using the integrity protection algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse.

The UE sets `ue-Type` to `relayUE` if it is acting as an NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay UE.

This is stated in the context:

> 4 &gt; include ue-Type and set it to relayUE if the UE is acting as NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay UE and to remoteUE otherwise;

The UE sets `sl-TxInterestedFreqList` to indicate **the frequency of the associated destination for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission**.

This is explicitly stated in the context:

> 5 > set sl-TxInterestedFreqList to indicate the frequency of the associated destination for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission;

The UE discards the NR sidelink communication related configuration of this destination.

Quoted from the context:  
> 2 &gt; discard the NR sidelink communication related configuration of this destination;

If the targetRAT-Type in the MobilityFromNRCommand is set to utra-fdd, the UE shall:

- consider inter-RAT mobility as initiated towards UTRA-FDD;
- forward the nas-SecurityParamFromNR to the upper layers, if included;
- access the target cell indicated in the inter-RAT message in accordance with the specifications of the target RAT.
